{"id": "EUVD-2026-59337", "enisaUuid": "a4827ca3-d8fa-368f-9ddc-4654d741f3b7", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nmd/raid10: fix writes_pending and barrier reference leaks on discard failures\n\nraid10_make_request() acquires a writes_pending reference with\nmd_write_start() before calling raid10_handle_discard(). Several failure\npaths in raid10_handle_discard() complete the bio and return without\nreleasing the corresponding reference, causing md_write_end() to be\nskipped.\n\nCall md_write_end() before returning from these failure paths to keep\nwrites_pending accounting balanced.\n\nAdditionally, discard split allocation failures can occur after\nwait_barrier() succeeds. Those paths return without calling\nallow_barrier(), leaking the associated barrier reference.\n\nRelease the barrier before returning from those paths.", "datePublished": "2026-08-15T05:56:51", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:44:55", "baseScore": 7.5, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/80ac31cce55432034a9eb98262c92ace7866e494", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/fea33968592559a55a3f5a96a6386bebcaf988a8", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/11b35d1906a7277a3d64afe34224133b44327328", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d1324b41dabd26787559efaeb430643c627c1eb0", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/393d687131d8aa8c7e4de2cb494438e145d20fc2"], "aliases": ["GHSA-cxhw-2fw5-695j", "CVE-2026-72438"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.46, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "2859d39e-5f3f-3eb5-941c-7f5c2b57ec94", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.17"}, {"id": "3cd1b6b3-bde9-33bc-8266-fa2dc6d14e62", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2"}, {"id": "3f7c827f-4376-3e31-8938-7c3a10d19aca", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.53"}, {"id": "4bc8c585-4b40-3a7b-9c15-627dfcb676e0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "57ce1072-15ff-3776-9c63-4387a6fdb2be", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "c9aa889b035fca4598ae985a0f0c76ebbb547ad2 <393d687131d8aa8c7e4de2cb494438e145d20fc2"}, {"id": "67b531c6-61b1-3279-8ab7-82c882f96a39", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.15.111 <5.16"}, {"id": "7df2fa37-71cc-3c5b-aebb-2f6e33c77d33", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "c9aa889b035fca4598ae985a0f0c76ebbb547ad2 <80ac31cce55432034a9eb98262c92ace7866e494"}, {"id": "9ce4b407-0975-3dd9-8a54-29b1318b9e1f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "c9aa889b035fca4598ae985a0f0c76ebbb547ad2 <11b35d1906a7277a3d64afe34224133b44327328"}, {"id": "b12d24b7-2022-3b40-8cba-3f0919a7f5e9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "c9aa889b035fca4598ae985a0f0c76ebbb547ad2 <fea33968592559a55a3f5a96a6386bebcaf988a8"}, {"id": "b1faa927-220f-37fb-948b-883998f9d715", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "c9aa889b035fca4598ae985a0f0c76ebbb547ad2 <d1324b41dabd26787559efaeb430643c627c1eb0"}, {"id": "b7250867-6c25-3fad-a8f3-9f6d7446ce60", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "d1c45cf8-2cda-3fef-bf10-e6764c2826a9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.111"}, {"id": "d6dfc7de-cfa4-38e4-be69-3a7d540c23bd", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.1.5"}, {"id": "fb84ebf7-61a5-3f54-99e7-268ce1499b6e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "39db562b3fedb93978a7e42dd216b306740959f8"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "9775300f-40b9-344c-b8e4-428